## Purpose
This document outlines how to analyze job descriptions and generate tailored application materials
## Input and Output Files
- **Input**: `applications/active/{company-name}/job-details/job-description.md`
- **Output**: 
  - `applications/active/{company-name}/job-details/requirements-analysis.md`
  - `applications/active/{company-name}/job-details/matching-skills.md`

## Analysis Process

### 1. Job Description Analysis
When analyzing a job description, the AI should:
- Extract all technical skills mentioned (not limited to a predefined list)
- Identify soft skills and interpersonal qualities
- Determine years of experience requirements
- Extract education requirements
- Identify key responsibilities and duties
- Recognize company values and culture indicators
- Extract industry-specific terminology and keywords

### 2. Requirements Analysis Document
Generate a requirements-analysis.md file with these sections:
```markdown
# Job Requirements Analysis

## Technical Skills
- [Technical Skill 1]: [Your level of proficiency, experience]
- [Technical Skill 2]: [Your level of proficiency, experience]
...

## Soft Skills
- [Soft Skill 1]: [Your level of proficiency, experience]
- [Soft Skill 2]: [Your level of proficiency, experience]
...

## Experience Requirements
- Years of Experience: [Required years]
- [Other experience requirements]: [How you meet this requirement]

## Education Requirements
- [Education Requirement]: [How you meet this requirement]

## Key Responsibilities
- [Responsibility 1]: [Relevant experience]
- [Responsibility 2]: [Relevant experience]
- [Responsibility 3]: [Relevant experience]

## Company Values Alignment
- [Value 1]: [How you demonstrate this value]
- [Value 2]: [How you demonstrate this value]
- [Value 3]: [How you demonstrate this value]
```

### 3. Skills Matching Analysis Document
Generate a matching-skills.md file with these sections:
```markdown
# Skills Matching Analysis

## Technical Skills Match
| Job Requirement | My Skill Level | Evidence/Example |
|----------------|---------------|------------------|
| [Skill 1] | [Your level] | [Specific example] |
| [Skill 2] | [Your level] | [Specific example] |
...

## Soft Skills Match
| Job Requirement | My Skill Level | Evidence/Example |
|----------------|---------------|------------------|
| [Skill 1] | [Your level] | [Specific example] |
| [Skill 2] | [Your level] | [Specific example] |
...

## Experience Match
| Job Requirement | My Experience | Gap Analysis |
|----------------|---------------|-------------|
| [Requirement] | [Your experience] | [Any gap and how to address] |

## Keywords for Resume/Cover Letter
- [keyword 1] (frequency)
- [keyword 2] (frequency)
...

## Overall Match Assessment
- **Technical Skills**: [Percentage match]
- **Soft Skills**: [Percentage match]
- **Experience**: [Percentage match]
- **Overall**: [Percentage match]

## Action Items
- [Action 1 to improve application]
- [Action 2 to improve application]
- [Action 3 to improve application]
```

## Usage Instructions

1. Create application structure:
   ```
   ./tools/scripts/create-application.sh company-name
   ```

2. Add job description to:
   ```
   applications/active/company-name/job-details/job-description.md
   ```

3. Use AI to analyze the job description by:
   - Copying the job description text
   - Asking the AI to "Analyze this job description and generate requirements-analysis.md and matching-skills.md files"
   - Providing your skills and experience information when prompted

4. Save the AI outputs to:
   ```
   applications/active/company-name/job-details/requirements-analysis.md
   applications/active/company-name/job-details/matching-skills.md
   ```

5. Use these analyses to tailor your resume and cover letter

## Advantages Over Script
- No limitation to predefined skill lists
- Better semantic understanding of requirements
- More accurate extraction of implicit requirements
- Personalized gap analysis and recommendations
- Ability to understand industry-specific terminology
- Improved keyword extraction with contextual understanding